**Every `--help` page `nxc` can render, captured** (nxf 6j6v.spjj, closed for the `nxc` tree by
6j6v.dvyq).

No gate watched this text before, and it had already bitten: removing `nxc threads expect` left clap
advertising the subcommand in `nxc threads --help`, user-visible, and nothing went red. The reason is
structural rather than an oversight — `xtask::docs::render_all` renders `nexus_flow_cli::command()`
and nothing else, so `docs/generated/` has no `nxc` subtree at all and `cargo xtask docs check` /
`docs coverage` cannot see this surface however carefully they run.

So the pages are goldens. Every leaf verb and every group node is here, which is what makes this a
MAP rather than a spot-check: a group page names its children (so a removed or added subcommand
shows up), and a leaf page names its flags (so a removed or added option does too). A verb that is
taken away and leaves its help behind now turns this file red.

Agent ergonomics is this project's stated measuring stick, and a help page naming a verb that no
longer exists is a false map, not a cosmetic defect: an agent reads it and then types something the
binary refuses.

A page that is REMOVED has to leave this file with its verb: regenerating would otherwise capture
clap's "unrecognized subcommand" as the page's expected output, and the map would quietly become a
map of doors that are shut. Delete the block; `tests/consolidated_entrances.rs` is where a removed
entrance's refusal is pinned.

Regenerate after an INTENDED surface change, and only then — read the diff before committing it:
`cargo build -p nxs && TRYCMD=overwrite cargo test -p nexus-chat --test golden`. The `nxs` build
first is load-bearing: `nxc` is a multicall alias of that binary, so a stale one would burn the
previous surface into these pages (the freshness gate in `golden.rs` refuses that outright).

```console
$ nxc --help
nexus-chat agent CLI

Usage: nxc [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init            Initialize chat in the current directory: ensure a `.nxs` workspace, register the `chat` module, then delegate the shared agent file + one SessionStart hook per active module to the `nxs` assembler (re-assembling every active module) — parity with `nxm init`
  agent-manifest  Emit nxc's declared contribution to the shared agent file (the prime command + the SessionStart hook) as data. `--json` is the machine contract the `nxs` umbrella assembles from
  list            Who can be addressed here, and what for. Without `--persona` a human sees the whole declared team — which is also what an app renders as its directory — while a running persona sees its own address book, recognised from its session. With `--persona` it is that persona's view, whoever is asking
  send            Open a conversation with a declared persona or channel: posts the first message, stamps a thread, and starts (or wakes) whoever is on the other side. Returns the thread id
  reply           Answer in a thread: posts into the thread's own channel and hands the turn back to whoever is on the other side of it
  threads         Thread quorum boards: `list` the caller's boards, or `show` one in full
  status          Where an operation stands: the whole thread TREE from its root down, across channel borders. `--thread` shows the one operation that thread belongs to; `--channel` the live operations that started in a channel; `--all` adds the finished ones; with none of them, everything still going on here
  search          Case-insensitive substring over message bodies in the caller's channels (bound LIKE), deterministically ordered
  session         The role-runtime internal↔real SDK session map
  transcript      The role session's Claude Agent SDK transcript: the normalized stream — assistant text, thinking, tool calls and their results, and any subagent activity they spawned
  machine         Which machine a chat runs on — a new one with `--to <persona>`, or `--thread <id>` — and whether sending now would ask instead: the machine, where that came from, whether it is online, and the machines that are. Writes nothing
  withdraw        Take back a commission — one still waiting for the working copy, or a round that is running
  resume          Take up an operation that stopped because the model was not available to it — an exhausted quota, a provider that was unreachable, a broken connection
  guide           Print an embedded, offline guide. Omit the topic to list the available ones
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json     Emit machine-readable JSON instead of human output
      --db <DB>  Use this sqlite db file directly instead of discovering `.nxs/` [env: NXC_DB=]
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

```

